=3D"markdown-content_markdown__cVmKc"><p>TIP:<br>
return result as 32 bits and take input as the same 32 bits<br>
No need to convert it to int anywhere<br>
In this problem you learn how to work with uint32_t,<br>
like if it were a string then too easy<br>
but by being this type, we work with shifts and bitwise operators</p>
<p>Exampe at end:<br>
some Defns:<br>
Left shift (&lt;&lt;): Moves bits to the left, adds zeros on the right, and=
 does not remove bits.<br>
Right shift (&gt;&gt;): Moves bits to the right, removes the least signific=
ant bit (rightmost bit), and adds zeros on the left for unsigned numbers.</=
p>
<p>Bitwise AND (&amp;): In the code n &amp; 1, this is used specifically to=
 isolate and extract the least significant bit (LSB) of n. It doesn't affec=
t the other bits in n.<br>
Bitwise OR (|): The | operator is used to append the extracted bit to resul=
t, modifying the LSB of result in each iteration, while leaving the other b=
its unchanged.</p>
<p>bitwise means : bit by bit<br>
n&amp;1 =3D=3D n &amp; (00...001) =3D=3D the last bit =3D=3D bit, which is =
single digit int;<br>
(result&lt;&lt;1) | bit =3D=3D (....0) | (....bit) =3D=3D (....bit);</p>
<p>Example:<br>
n =3D 1101<br>
left shift:  n&lt;&lt;1 =3D=3D 11010 (left shifts by 1 =3D adds one zero)<b=
r>
right shift: n&gt;&gt;1 =3D=3D 0110;<br>
n &amp; 1 =3D 1101 &amp; 0001 =3D 0001 =3D=3D 1; as i put bit as int<br>
if i apply n =3D n &gt;&gt; 1<br>
then n =3D 0110<br>
now n&amp;1 =3D 0110 &amp; 0001 =3D 0000 =3D 0;</p>
<p>result =3D 0 (say) and bit =3D 1 (say)<br>
res &lt;&lt; 1 =3D=3D 00  (moves res to left by adding 0 at end)<br>
(res &lt;&lt; 1) | bit =3D (00) | (01) =3D 01;<br>
basically by doing the left shift we add 0 to end of res, then do the "or" =
so the last 0<br>
newly added becomes the bit.<br>
so 00 became 01.</p>
<p>res =3D (res&lt;&lt;1) | bit;<br>
is the same as:<br>
res =3D res&lt;&lt;1;<br>
res =3D res | bit.</p>
<p>its not easy for first time ofc,<br>
I had to see solution<br>
BTW this is my first ever tipp!!<br>
Hope it helps</p></div></div><span style=3D"font-size: 0px; line-height: 0;=
